Highly advanced, automated CI/CD pipeline that will:

Sync over 100GB of untouched Google source code.

Inject Kali Linux penetration testing drivers (Wi-Fi and HID).

### just KenrelSU Next for now, susFS author needs to do some updates ### Inject Next-Gen root and stealth mechanisms (KernelSU Next + SUSFS).

Expose all the hidden battery, thermal, and CPU hardware registers.

Compile the massive 6.1 kernel using Google's Bazel system.

Package it neatly into an AnyKernel3 zip.


Use at your own risk. Built for Pixel 8 Pro running Android 16 on the May update. 
If you are not overfly familiar with flashing kernels, do not attempt. 

Otherwise..

Flash and enjoy! 

-stoag



To utilize external wifi adapters in your nethunter terminal you will need these commands. This prevents conflicts with your internal adapters.

Atheros Based Alfa Adapters:
insmod /vendor/lib/modules/ath9k_htc.ko

Ralink/MediaTek: 
insmod /vendor/lib/modules/rt2800usb.ko

Realtek: 
insmod /vendor/lib/modules/rtl8187.ko



